# COVESA VSS overlay — proposed signals for fleet data points that VSS cannot carry
# and that should NOT be derived by consumers.
# Companion to tmp/fmd-vss-gaps/README.md, the Fleet Management Data sheet (v4.6) and the
# an OEM partner's VSS mapping review (Nov 2026).
# Base: VSS master after 6.1 (includes ACEA FMS v5, PR #932; checked at 9dd09ad8).
# Apply with vss-tools: --overlays tmp/fmd-vss-gaps/fmd-gaps.vspec
# Status: PROPOSAL for discussion in the COVESA Commercial and Fleet Vehicle Group; not adopted.
#
# Selection rule: a value is proposed only if at least one holds —
#   (1) the ECU computes it from information not exposed elsewhere in VSS,
#   (2) it is a lifetime counter a later-installed or intermittently connected consumer cannot rebuild,
#   (3) regulation already fixes its meaning,
#   (4) it is safety-critical or claim-relevant, so a heuristic is not acceptable,
#   (5) deriving it needs high-rate or bulky inputs.
# Values that can be derived cheaply from existing signals are documented as derivation rules
# in README.md instead.

#
# Collision — OEM partner crash type signal; FNOL / emergency dispatch
#
Vehicle.Safety.CollisionType:
  datatype: string
  type: sensor
  allowed: ['UNKNOWN', 'NONE', 'FRONT', 'REAR', 'LEFT', 'RIGHT', 'ROLLOVER', 'MULTIPLE']
  description: Principal direction of the most recent collision detected by the vehicle.
  comment: Determined by the restraint control module from its crash sensors. NONE indicates no collision detected in
           the current power cycle. MULTIPLE indicates more than one impact direction in the same event. Complements
           Vehicle.Safety.Rollover. Rules (1), (4), (5). Primary consumers - emergency dispatch, first notice of loss.

#
# Traction battery thermal event — OEM partner battery fire alarm
#
Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.ThermalEventState:
  datatype: string
  type: sensor
  allowed: ['UNKNOWN', 'NONE', 'RISK', 'DETECTED']
  description: Indicates whether the traction battery is at risk of, or has detected, a thermal event.
  comment: Determined by the battery management system (e.g. temperature, voltage, gas or pressure sensing). UN GTR 20
           requires a warning to occupants for a thermal event, so the state already exists in vehicles. Earlier warning
           than Vehicle.Safety.IsFire. Rules (1), (3), (4).

#
# Aftertreatment — FMD "DPF regen status"; OEM partner DPF warning
#
Vehicle.Powertrain.CombustionEngine.DieselParticulateFilter.RegenerationStatus:
  datatype: string
  type: sensor
  allowed: ['NOT_ACTIVE', 'ACTIVE', 'NEEDED']
  description: State of diesel particulate filter regeneration.
  comment: NEEDED = regeneration required but not running (e.g. parked regeneration pending). Corresponds to J1939
           SPN 3700. A temperature heuristic cannot distinguish passive from active regeneration or detect NEEDED. Rule (1).

Vehicle.Powertrain.CombustionEngine.DieselParticulateFilter.SootLoad:
  datatype: uint8
  type: sensor
  unit: percent
  min: 0
  max: 100
  description: Soot load of the diesel particulate filter, relative to the regeneration threshold.
  comment: Corresponds to J1939 SPN 3719. DeltaPressure alone is not a reliable proxy because it depends on exhaust
           flow. Rule (1).

#
# DEF — OEM partner AdBlue text warnings; FMD "Aftertreatment fuel used"
#
Vehicle.Powertrain.CombustionEngine.DieselExhaustFluid.TotalConsumption:
  datatype: double
  type: sensor
  unit: l
  min: 0
  description: Diesel exhaust fluid consumed since the vehicle was built.
  comment: Reported from the dosing control, not from tank level (level is coarse and affected by refills and slosh).
           The DEF-to-fuel ratio is a common indicator of emission-system tampering. Rules (1), (2).

Vehicle.Powertrain.CombustionEngine.DieselExhaustFluid.Inducement:
  type: branch
  description: Driver inducement system for the selective catalytic reduction (SCR) emission control.

Vehicle.Powertrain.CombustionEngine.DieselExhaustFluid.Inducement.Level:
  datatype: string
  type: sensor
  allowed: ['UNKNOWN', 'NONE', 'WARNING', 'LOW_LEVEL', 'SEVERE']
  description: Current stage of the driver inducement system.
  comment: WARNING = driver warning only. LOW_LEVEL = performance restriction (e.g. torque reduction). SEVERE = severe
           restriction (e.g. speed limit or no restart). Stages and thresholds are defined by emission regulation and may
           differ by market. Rules (1), (3).

Vehicle.Powertrain.CombustionEngine.DieselExhaustFluid.Inducement.Reasons:
  datatype: string[]
  type: sensor
  allowed: ['DEF_LEVEL', 'DEF_QUALITY', 'DOSING_INTERRUPTION', 'CONSUMPTION_DEVIATION', 'EGR_VALVE', 'MONITORING_FAILURE', 'OTHER']
  description: Reasons currently causing the inducement warning or restriction.
  comment: Replaces per-reason driver text messages with one list. Empty when Level is NONE.

Vehicle.Powertrain.CombustionEngine.DieselExhaustFluid.Inducement.DistanceToRestriction:
  datatype: uint32
  type: sensor
  unit: m
  description: Remaining distance before the next inducement stage takes effect.

Vehicle.Powertrain.CombustionEngine.DieselExhaustFluid.Inducement.TimeToRestriction:
  datatype: uint32
  type: sensor
  unit: s
  description: Remaining engine operating time before the next inducement stage takes effect.

#
# Idle fuel — FMD "Total fuel used while idling", "Idling hydrogen fuel used"
#
Vehicle.Powertrain.FuelSystem.TotalIdleConsumption:
  datatype: double
  type: sensor
  unit: l
  min: 0
  description: Liquid fuel consumed while the engine was idling, since the vehicle was built.
  comment: Idle counterpart of FuelSystem.TotalConsumption, using the ECU's idle definition. Corresponds to J1939 SPN 236.
           Consumers wanting one cross-OEM idle definition may instead derive it (see README). Rule (2).

Vehicle.Powertrain.FuelSystem.TotalIdleConsumptionGaseous:
  datatype: double
  type: sensor
  unit: kg
  min: 0
  description: Gaseous fuel consumed while the engine was idling, since the vehicle was built.
  comment: Idle counterpart of FuelSystem.TotalConsumptionGaseous; covers CNG, LNG and H2. Rule (2).

#
# Bidirectional charging — FMD "AC / DC charging energy out"
#
Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Charging.AccumulatedDischargedEnergy:
  datatype: float
  type: sensor
  unit: kWh
  min: 0
  description: Energy delivered from the vehicle through the charging inlet to an external load or the grid (V2G, V2L),
               over the lifetime of the vehicle.
  comment: Measured at the inlet, so it differs from battery-side energy by conversion losses. Needed for grid
           settlement and battery warranty. Rule (2).

#
# Tire monitoring — OEM partner TPMS malfunction warnings
#
Vehicle.Chassis.Axle.Row1.Wheel.Left.Tire.PressureStatus:
  datatype: string
  type: sensor
  allowed: ['UNKNOWN', 'NORMAL', 'LOW', 'CRITICALLY_LOW', 'HIGH', 'FAST_LEAK', 'SENSOR_ERROR']
  description: Tire pressure monitoring status for this tire.
  comment: Determined by the TPMS. Fast leak needs closely spaced samples and sensor error cannot be derived from Pressure.
           Upstream this would be added once in the Tire definition for all wheel instances (see open VSS PR 940 on wheel
           designation). Rules (1), (3), (5).

#
# Battery cell temperature extremes — OEM partner max/min cell temperature index
#
Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Temperature.IdMax:
  datatype: uint16
  type: sensor
  description: Identifier of the battery cell with highest temperature.
  comment: Identifier is supposed to be relative index of the cell, starting with 0 the first cell. Mirrors
           CellVoltage.IdMax; avoids sending the full CellTemperature array to find one index. Rule (5).

Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Temperature.IdMin:
  datatype: uint16
  type: sensor
  description: Identifier of the battery cell with lowest temperature.
  comment: Identifier is supposed to be relative index of the cell, starting with 0 the first cell. Mirrors
           CellVoltage.IdMin. Rule (5).
